# Shipping default (SITE 00)

Founder codes primarily from **mobile**. Default workflow: **code lands on `main` quickly**, but every change still gets a **PR for history and review**.

## Default (unless the user opts out)

1. Work on a feature branch (`cursor/<descriptive-name>-796f`).
2. Commit, push, and **open a PR** to `main` (title + short body describing what changed).
3. **Merge the PR to `main` in the same agent session** after push — do not leave it open for the founder to merge manually.
4. Resolve merge conflicts with `main` **before** merging (fetch `origin/main` first).
5. After merge, confirm `main` has the commits; remind founder that **site00.com** still needs GoDaddy deploy (GitHub Actions artifact/ZIP or FTP) unless auto-FTP is enabled.
6. **Session close:** Before your final message, follow `.cursor/rules/session-close.mdc` — prose summary + conclusion code box + deploy links (each on its own line). Merging the PR is not the end of the session.

## When NOT to auto-merge

- User says **"draft PR"**, **"don't merge yet"**, or **"wait for my review"**.
- Merge conflicts involve **conflicting intents** (not trivial line collisions) — fix if simple; otherwise report and leave PR open.
- User explicitly wants to merge from the GitHub app.

## PR role

The PR is a **receipt** (diff, description, CI), not a waiting room. Founder may review on the GitHub app after merge.

## Do not

- Push directly to `main` while skipping the PR (unless user explicitly requests direct-to-main with no PR).
